The controller owns scheduling, retries, ownership, recovery and completion deterministically. Hermes is a disposable implementation/diagnosis worker, not the sole holder of the plan or execution state.

Do not promise impossible completion. Host power loss, unavailable credentials, external approvals, permanent provider outages and unavailable physical hardware can prevent progress. Persist these honestly, continue unrelated eligible work, automatically resume retryable waits, and surface genuine human blockers. Never substitute fake evidence, silently weaken the specification, or call a blocked project complete.

